      "wk-ingredients": {
        "type": "wk-ingredients",
        "settings": {
          "eyebrow": "What's inside, and why",
          "heading": "Every ingredient, chosen for a reason",
          "subhead": "No proprietary blends. No fairy dust. No hiding behind vague labels. Every active in Womankind is clearly named, fully dosed, and selected for the specific role it plays in supporting you through perimenopause—with ingredient choices grounded in published research, not marketing fluff.",
          "supp_button_label": "See full supplement facts",
          "ing1_name": "Ashwagandha root",
          "ing1_dose": "200 mg",
          "ing1_desc": "A standardised adaptogen for the stress response — supporting steadier mood and calmer days through the transition.*",
          "ing2_name": "Black cohosh",
          "ing2_dose": "100 mg",
          "ing2_desc": "Standardised to 5% triterpene glycosides — the botanical most studied for hot flashes and night sweats.*",
          "ing3_name": "Red clover",
          "ing3_dose": "100 mg",
          "ing3_desc": "40% isoflavones — plant compounds that gently support hormonal balance as estrogen shifts.*",
          "ing4_name": "Chasteberry",
          "ing4_dose": "100 mg",
          "ing4_desc": "Also known as Vitex — traditionally used to support hormonal rhythm and the month-to-month patterns that shift in perimenopause.*",
          "ing7_name": "Vitamins B6, D3 & E",
          "ing7_dose": "2 mg · 20 mcg · 15 mg",
          "ing7_desc": "Foundational support for mood, bone, and cellular defense — with D3 sourced from lichen, not sheep's wool.*",
          "ing8_name": "Probiotic blend",
          "ing8_dose": "10B CFU",
          "ing8_desc": "A 6-strain Lacto/Bifido blend that feeds the estrobolome — the gut bacteria that metabolise estrogen.*"
        }
      },
      "wk-ingredients-3": {
        "type": "wk-ingredients-3",
        "settings": {
          "ing1_desc": "<span style=\"display:block;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C9653F;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;\">Why it’s here</span>Perimenopause can make everyday stress feel harder to manage—and poor sleep can make that cycle even more difficult. Ashwagandha is an adaptogenic botanical traditionally used to support the body’s response to stress.<br><br>Womankind includes ashwagandha to support a steadier stress response, calmer mood, and a greater sense of emotional balance during hormonal change.*",
          "ing2_desc": "<span style=\"display:block;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C9653F;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;\">Why it’s here</span>Black cohosh is one of the most researched botanicals traditionally used for menopause-related symptoms, particularly hot flashes and night sweats.<br><br>We include it to provide targeted support for temperature regulation and to help make hot flashes and night sweats feel less intense or disruptive for some women.*",
          "ing3_desc": "<span style=\"display:block;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C9653F;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;\">Why it’s here</span>Red clover naturally contains isoflavones—plant compounds that have been studied for their relationship to menopause-related changes.<br><br>Womankind includes red clover as part of a broader formula designed to support comfort, temperature balance, and overall wellbeing as your hormones change during perimenopause.*",
          "ing4_desc": "<span style=\"display:block;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C9653F;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;\">Why it’s here</span>Chasteberry has a long history of traditional use in women’s health and has been studied for menstrual-cycle-related symptoms.<br><br>We include it to support a steadier cycle rhythm and help you navigate the changing patterns that can come with perimenopause.*",
          "ing7_desc": "<span style=\"display:block;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C9653F;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;\">Why they’re here</span>Perimenopause support is not only about botanicals. Vitamins also help provide foundational nutritional support during a period when sleep, mood, energy, and overall wellbeing may feel less predictable.<br><br>Vitamin B6 contributes to normal psychological function and the regulation of hormonal activity.<br>Vitamin D3 supports normal bones, muscle function, and immune function.<br>Vitamin E contributes to protection of cells from oxidative stress.<br><br>Together, they provide foundational support for mood, bones, immune function, and everyday energy.*",
          "ing8_desc": "<span style=\"display:block;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C9653F;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;\">Why it’s here</span>Your gut is involved in digestion, nutrient absorption, and the way the body processes many compounds—including hormones and hormone metabolites.<br><br>Womankind includes a 10-billion-CFU probiotic blend to support a healthy gut environment and the body’s natural hormone-related pathways.*"
        }
      },
