          "subhead": "No scripts. No stock photos. Just women sharing what changed after making Womankind part of their daily routine.",
          "footer_text": "Scroll to see more →",
          "card1_title": "“Cooler nights at last”",
          "card1_body": "“By week three, the night sweats were less frequent and I was sleeping more deeply. I started waking up feeling like myself again.”",
          "card1_cite": "— Renée, 45",
          "card2_title": "“I stopped planning around hot flashes”",
          "card2_body": "“I carried a fan everywhere and always knew the coolest seat in the room. A month in, the flushes started spacing out—and I stopped planning my day around them.”",
          "card2_cite": "— Dani, 49",
          "card3_title": "“The bloating finally calmed down”",
          "card3_body": "“Three weeks in, my stomach felt settled for the first time in a year. I didn’t expect that to be one of the first changes I noticed.”",
          "card3_cite": "— Grace L., 47",
          "card4_title": "“My afternoon fog lifted”",
          "card4_body": "“The afternoon haze is gone. I can follow a thought through a whole meeting without losing the thread.”",
          "card4_cite": "— Cass, 51",
          "card5_title": "“The little things stay little now”",
          "card5_body": "“I don’t feel as reactive or overwhelmed. My family noticed the difference before I did, honestly.”",
          "card5_cite": "— Lauren, 47",
          "card6_title": "“I feel like myself again”",
          "card6_body": "“First the 2am wake-ups eased. Then, sometime in month two, I caught myself feeling like me again.”",
          "card6_cite": "— Rowan, 46"
        }
      },
      "wk-faq": {
        "type": "wk-faq",
        "settings": {
          "eyebrow": "Questions, answered",
          "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
          "subhead": "",
          "q1": "Will this actually work for me, or is it another placebo?",
          "a1": "We built this formula because that's exactly what we refused to sell. Every active is at a clinically-relevant dose, printed on the label — no proprietary blends, no hidden under-dosing, zero sugar. The formula works on the root: the brain's thermostat and the gut-hormone axis. And if it doesn't work for you, it costs you nothing — we back that with our 90-day guarantee.",
          "q2": "Can I take it with my medications — and is it safe every day, long-term?",
          "a2": "There are no known interactions with common prescriptions like SSRIs, thyroid medication, blood pressure medication, or birth control — but if you take daily medication, please run it past your prescriber first. It's a quick conversation. For long-term daily use: yes. Our doses have established safety data, our six probiotic strains are among the most studied in the world, and every batch is third-party tested. Vegan, made in Europe, sugar-free.",
          "q3": "Does this contain hormones? I can’t take HRT.",
          "a3": "No. There are no hormones in this. Not estrogen. Not progesterone. Not DHEA. Not “secretly kind of HRT.” || If you can’t take hormone therapy — or you don’t want to — that’s exactly who this was built for. Botanicals at researched doses, not a hormone in a gummy. || If you are already on HRT and want to add this, that’s a conversation with your clinician. Bring them the label. That’s why every milligram is printed.",
          "q4": "How long until I feel something — and what if I don’t?",
          "a4": "Some women notice quieter nights or spacing flashes around weeks 3–4. For a lot of people the clearer shift is closer to weeks 6–8. Full effect is a 30–90 day window. That’s the formula, not a delay tactic. || That’s why most women start with the 3-month supply — you’re covered for the window, and it’s the better daily price. If you’d rather begin with one bottle, you can. Same gummies. Same 90-day guarantee. You can add more whenever you’re ready. || Take two a day. Give it a real chance. If your nights, heat, mood, or energy haven’t moved in a way that matters to you, you don’t pay. Keep the bottle. You don’t need to write us an essay.",
          "q5": "Is it too late for me? I'm past 50.",
          "a5": "No. The systems our formula supports — the hypothalamus-thermostat axis and the estrobolome — don't switch off at menopause. Women in their mid-50s and beyond report the same pattern: flushes down from a dozen a day to a handful a week, dry sheets, real sleep. We built this for perimenopause <em>and</em> beyond. The only version of too late is another year you didn't have to spend soaked and sleepless.",
          "q6": "How does the subscription work — and can I cancel anytime?",
          "a6": "Subscribing gets you the best price with free shipping, and you're always in control: pause, skip, or cancel anytime, no hoops. You can also order a one-time purchase if you'd rather try it first. Our honest take: the real results land at month 3, and subscribers pay the lowest price to get there.",
          "q7": "What if it doesn't work for me?",
          "a7": "Email us within 90 days for a full refund — no returns, no forms, no fine print. The gut-hormone axis doesn't reset overnight, and a 30-day guarantee would ask you to quit before the shift happens. We give you a full three months because that's what your body actually needs — and we're betting on you, not on the fine print.",
          "q8": "What if I already take HRT, or other menopause supplements?",
          "a8": "This is not HRT and it does not replace HRT. || Some women use it because they can’t take hormones. Some use it because they don’t want to. Some are already on a prescription and want a non-hormonal option for sleep and heat — that is between you and your clinician. Bring them the label. || If you’re already taking other menopause blends, don’t stack three things and then guess which one did what. Pick a protocol. Give it 90 days.",
          "q9": "",
          "a9": ""
        }
      },
